 ## Overview
-Energy Region Compositing is a volume rendering technique that composites multiple energy volumes within a specific region of interest defined by a magnitude volume, applying a threshold to energy intensity before compositing [S1, unofficial]. It renders a volume using multiple energy volumes, blending colors based on normalized intensities above a threshold [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard direct volume ray casting which uses a single transfer function for opacity and color, this method uses a magnitude volume to gate visibility and blends distinct energy contributions based on their relative intensity ratios [S1, unofficial].
+Energy Region Compositing is a volume rendering technique that composites multiple energy-specific volumes within a specific region of interest defined by a magnitude volume [S1, unofficial]. It applies a threshold to energy intensity before compositing, blending colors based on normalized intensities above that threshold [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard direct volume ray casting which integrates opacity and color along a single scalar field, this method selectively renders energy contributions only where the magnitude volume indicates presence, effectively masking out background noise or irrelevant regions [S1, unofficial].
 
